#668: Proof-Theoretic Complexity x AIT\n\n## L3 MeTTa Encoding\n\n### Type Declarations (10)\n\n(declare-type ProofSystem)\n(declare-type ProofTree)\n(declare-type Theorem)\n(declare-type Language)\n(declare-type Axioms)\n(declare-type Rules)\n(declare-type Ordinal)\n(declare-type Natural)\n(declare-type LogSize)\n(declare-type Signature)\n\n### D1-D7 Typed Atoms\n\n; D1: Proof system = (Language, Axioms, Rules)\n(|- ((--> ProofSystem (x Language Axioms Rules)) (stv 1.0 0.9)))\n\n; D2: Proof tree = (Theorem, List ProofTree)\n(|- ((--> ProofTree (x Theorem (List ProofTree))) (stv 1.0 0.9)))\n\n; D3: Ordinal height h(pi) : Natural\n(|- ((--> (OrdinalHeight $pi) Natural) (stv 1.0 0.9)))\n\n; D4: Proof size s(pi) : Natural\n(|- ((--> (ProofSize $pi) Natural) (stv 1.0 0.9)))\n\n; D5: Kolmogorov complexity K(T) : Natural\n(|- ((--> (KolmogorovComplexity $T) Natural) (stv 1.0 0.9)))\n\n; D6: Signature size |Sigma| : Natural\n(|- ((--> (SigSize $Sigma) Natural) (stv 1.0 0.9)))\n\n; D7: Shortest proof pi_T of T : ProofTree (conjectural existence)\n(|- ((--> (ShortestProof $T) ProofTree) (stv 0.5 0.9)))\n\n### C1: Height-Size Decomposition\n\n; C1 Upper Bound (PROVEN): K(T) <= c_h * h(pi_T) * log|Sigma| + c_s * s(pi_T) * log|Sigma| + O(1)\n; Program encoding proof tree needs height-dependent branching bits + size-dependent label bits\n(|- ((==> (and (IsShortestProof $pi $T)\n              (IsProofSystem $Sigma))\n         (<= (KolmogorovComplexity $T)\n             (+ (* (* c_h (OrdinalHeight $pi)) (LogSig (SigSize $Sigma)))\n                (* (* c_s (ProofSize $pi)) (LogSig (SigSize $Sigma)))))) (stv 1.0 0.95))\n          ((IsShortestProof $pi $T) (stv 1.0 0.9))\n          ((IsProofSystem $Sigma) (stv 1.0 0.9)))\n\n; C1 Lower Bound (CONJECTURAL): K(T) >= c_h * h(pi_T) * log|Sigma| + c_s * s(pi_T) * log|Sigma| - O(1)\n(|- ((==> (and (IsShortestProof $pi $T)\n              (IsProofSystem $Sigma))\n         (>= (KolmogorovComplexity $T)\n             (- (+ (* (* c_h (OrdinalHeight $pi)) (LogSig (SigSize $Sigma)))\n                   (* (* c_s (ProofSize $pi)) (LogSig (SigSize $Sigma))))\n                const_O1))) (stv 0.5 0.9))\n          ((IsShortestProof $pi $T) (stv 1.0 0.9))\n          ((IsProofSystem $Sigma) (stv 1.0 0.9)))\n\n### C2: Overhead Computability (CONJECTURAL)\n; K(T) - c_h * h * log|Sigma| is computably approximable from above only\n(|~ ((Implication (Inheritance $T Theorem)\n         (ApproximableFromAbove (- (KolmogorovComplexity $T)\n                                   (* c_h (OrdinalHeight (ShortestProof $T)))))) (stv 0.5 0.9))\n          ((Inheritance $T Theorem) (stv 1.0 0.9)))\n\n### C3: Ordinal-Coefficient Stability (CONJECTURAL)\n; If alpha(Sigma1) < alpha(Sigma2) then c_h(Sigma1) <= c_h(Sigma2)\n(|~ ((Implication (and (Inheritance $Sigma1 ProofSystem)\n                        (Inheritance $Sigma2 ProofSystem)\n                        (< (ProofOrdinal $Sigma1) (ProofOrdinal $Sigma2)))\n         (<= (CoeffHeight $Sigma1) (CoeffHeight $Sigma2))) (stv 0.5 0.9))\n          ((Inheritance $Sigma1 ProofSystem) (stv 1.0 0.9))\n          ((Inheritance $Sigma2 ProofSystem) (stv 1.0 0.9)))\n\n### C4: Height-Size Tradeoff (CONJECTURAL)\n; Exist theorem families with h=O(1), s=Omega(n) and vice versa\n(|~ ((Implication (Inheritance $T_n Theorem)\n         (or (and (= (OrdinalHeight (ShortestProof $T_n)) const_O1)\n                  (>= (ProofSize (ShortestProof $T_n)) $n))\n             (and (>= (OrdinalHeight (ShortestProof $T_n)) $n)\n                  (= (ProofSize (ShortestProof $T_n)) const_O1)))) (stv 0.5 0.9))\n          ((Inheritance $T_n Theorem) (stv 1.0 0.9)))\n\n### C5: Phase Transition (CONJECTURAL)\n; As alpha(Sigma) crosses epsilon_0 or Gamma_0, ratio c_h/c_s jumps\n(|~ ((Implication (and (Inheritance $Sigma ProofSystem)\n                        (> (ProofOrdinal $Sigma) epsilon_0))\n         (> (RatioHeightToSize $Sigma) prev_ratio))) (stv 0.5 0.9))\n          ((Inheritance $Sigma ProofSystem) (stv 1.0 0.9)))\n\n### Caveats (5)\n; Caveat 1: Constants c_h, c_s depend on proof system and universal TM\n; Caveat 2: Lower bound direction of C1 is unproven for any natural proof system\n; Caveat 3: ShortestProof existence is not computable (halting problem)\n; Caveat 4: Ordinal height for finite proofs equals natural number height; ordinal structure only emerges for infinitary systems\n; Caveat 5: The decomposition may not be additive for proof systems with non-uniform rule arity\n\n### Cross-References (8)\n; #354 STE x RLCT: approximation vs compression analogy\n; #8 foundational RLCT framework\n; #16 Watanabe RLCT generalization bound\n; Garrabrant (2016) logical induction: market-based, not proof complexity\n; Solomonoff (1964): universal prior, program length only\n; Pudlak (1998): proof complexity lower bounds, no AIT connection\n; Curry-Howard: proofs as programs, height as type complexity\n; genesis_proof_theory.metta: proof theory MeTTa foundations\n\n### Status\n; C1 upper bound: PROVEN (stv 1.0 0.95)\n; C1 lower bound: CONJECTURAL (stv 0.5 0.9)\n; C2-C5: CONJECTURAL (stv 0.5 0.9)\n; L0-L1-L2-L3 pipeline COMPLETE\n; Next: L4 summary + L5 catalog append